# Nov 16 2026 (KPC owner): the answer-key RULE FILES are hashed byte for byte by
# .github/scripts/kpc_key_freeze.py (rules_hash), and that hash is what the 2-fer key gate
# compares against every key build. Git for Windows writes CRLF by default, so without these
# lines a Windows checkout of this very commit sees different bytes and works out a different
# rules hash than the Linux build did -- and the gate then calls every green key stale.
# rules_hash also levels line endings itself, so this file is the second lock, not the only one.
# ADD A NEW RULE FILE HERE when you add one to RULE_FILES in kpc_key_freeze.py.

